glad 2.0.5 - an OpenGL/EGL/WGL loader, generated rather than written.

The generator and its output are distributed under:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: (WTFPL OR CC0-1.0) AND Apache-2.0

which is the line every generated file carries at its top. The Apache-2.0 part
covers the Khronos specification data the generator reads; the loader code
itself is public domain under either WTFPL or CC0, at your option.

Upstream: https://github.com/Dav1dde/glad

WHY IT IS HERE. Chimera reaches OpenGL from C# for its own display. This copy
is for the engine's GPU bridge (docs/gpu-bridge.md), which answers a sandboxed
core's GL calls on a real context and therefore needs the entry points in C.
On Windows that is not a convenience: opengl32.dll exports OpenGL 1.1 and
nothing else, so everything a modern renderer calls has to be fetched at
runtime through wglGetProcAddress, and a loader is the only way to have it.

This is the same generated copy PCSX2 vendors, so the two sides of the bridge
agree about types and entry points by construction.
